bjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the exact proving commands: the monkeypatch/fixture target used to delay (6 s) and hang the background run, and the concrete 4-way concurrency invocation (e.g. `pytest -n 4 --count 20 ...` or a named loop).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.675,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"passes with the background run delayed 6 s, fails when the run never settles, and passes 20 of 20 runs at 4-way concurrency\"","Only one command is given: `pytest ... -k mcp_run_workflow`; no flags or fixture for delay or concurrency."],"finding":"The Testing section's discriminating checks ('delayed 6 s', 'run never settles') name no injection point or command. The 4-way concurrency run names no harness (pytest-xdist -n 4, a shell loop, or pytest-repeat). These checks are therefore not reproducible from the plan.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f894b1ed09575de4b","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing","norm_id":"ne3d9b55ab8ada438","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer cannot re-run the delay probe because it is unclear what was patched (the workflow runner, the executor, or the status store).","A delay injected after the completion signal fires would exercise nothing (fixture invalidity)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative