4e5154.' Keep the 20/20 load run as a supporting regression check, not the primary proof.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the chosen wait mechanism (e.g. join/Event on the background run) and the explicit upper bound used to fail the never-settles case, with a rationale for why that bound is not load-sensitive.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.734,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"waits on the run's own completion signal or a state change, not a fixed 5-second wall clock, and still fails when the run never settles\""],"finding":"The wait mechanism is left as an either/or ('completion signal or a state change'), and the bound that makes the test fail when the run never settles is unstated. Waiting on a completion signal with no timeout hangs instead of failing. Any timeout is itself a wall-clock deadline, so the plan should state its value or source.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f78ee2023f82362e0","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1","norm_id":"n8da571a522de6085","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer joins the thread with no timeout. The never-settles case hangs CI rather than failing with 'background run never settled'.","An implementer simply raises the poll budget to 10 s. This is still a fixed wall clock and still load-sensitive."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add to AC1 that, after the wait, the test still observes the run's terminal state via `get_workflow_status`, and still asserts that `run_workflow` returns before completion.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Test name: \"test_mcp_run_workflow_is_async_and_pollable\"","AC1 allows waiting on \"the run's own completion signal\", which may bypass the MCP status tool."],"finding":"Nothing requires the rewritten test to keep asserting the async/pollable contract through `get_workflow_status`, the behavior the test is named for. Switching to waiting on an internal completion signal could drop the MCP polling assertions while still satisfying AC1.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe4a12ed980f28b59","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1; tests/interfaces/store/test_workflow_entrypoints.py::test_mcp_run_workflow_is_async_and_pollable","norm_id":"n20d1a2ff43310401","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The test joins the background thread and then checks results directly, never calling `get_workflow_status` to observe the terminal state."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Append to AC1: '...and the test still asserts run_workflow returns immediately and get_workflow_status reports the terminal state after the wait.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Replace or augment AC2 with a discriminating AC: the test passes when the background run is artificially delayed past 5 s (e.g. 6 s) and fails on the unmodified test under that same delay.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3","E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7437,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"It then passed 26 of 26 runs on unmodified `origin/main` ... 16 runs of each arm were 4-way concurrent.\"","AC2: \"The test passes 20 of 20 runs under 4-way concurrent load.\"","Testing: \"passes with the background run delayed 6 s\" — not reflected in the ACs"],"finding":"AC2 ('passes 20 of 20 runs under 4-way concurrent load') cannot tell the fixed test from the broken one. The plan's own observation says unmodified origin/main already passed 26/26 runs, 16 of them 4-way concurrent. A test that still has the fixed 5 s wall clock would therefore satisfy AC2. The check that actually separates old from new appears only in the Testing prose ('passes with the background run delayed 6 s'). It is not an acceptance criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f47ff745c50d15f9a","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC2; Testing section","norm_id":"n1e68db832b56f33d","priority":0.2063,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A fix that only raises the poll count, or does nothing, still closes green on AC2 because the flake reproduces rarely."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC: 'With the background run delayed 6 s (monkeypatched), the modified test passes and the original 50×0.1 s loop fails.' Keep 20/20 at 4-way load as a secondary smoke check only.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the completion signal the test will wait on, and require that the test still asserts the terminal status via get_workflow_status (the public poll API) after that signal.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3","E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Test name: test_mcp_run_workflow_is_async_and_pollable","AC1: \"waits on the run's own completion signal or a state change\" — no mechanism named, no requirement that get_workflow_status is still asserted"],"finding":"The plan never names the 'run's own completion signal' the test will wait on. The test exists to prove that MCP run_workflow is async AND pollable through get_workflow_status. Suppose the new wait blocks on an internal thread/future/event instead of driving get_workflow_status. The test would then stop exercising the public polling contract, and polling could break while the test stays green. The plan does not commit to still asserting a terminal status through get_workflow_status after the signal fires.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f92552588bc8c6a12","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1 ('waits on the run's own completion signal or a state change')","norm_id":"nf111733d6910bd36","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The implementer joins the background thread directly; get_workflow_status regresses to never report a terminal state, and the test still passes."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the bound on the new wait (a generous hang guard, e.g. tens of seconds, distinct from a perf deadline) and that exceeding it fails with the existing 'background run never settled' assertion rather than hanging.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: \"...not a fixed 5-second wall clock, and still fails when the run never settles.\"","No timeout/bound or failure message specified for the new wait"],"finding":"AC1 requires that the test 'still fails when the run never settles', but the plan does not say what bounds the wait. If the test waits on a completion signal with no bound, a never-settling run will hang the suite (worker stall or CI job timeout) rather than fail with a clear message. If some bound remains, the plan should state it is deliberately generous, i.e. a hang guard and not a performance deadline. Otherwise it is unclear how the new wait differs from the 5 s ceiling it replaces.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0dae52d2e2c58b6e","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1; Testing ('fails when the run never settles')","norm_id":"nbf85fbe73b7a45ca","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression makes the background run deadlock; the test blocks indefinitely and xdist/CI reports a job timeout instead of 'background run never settled'."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a short Approach note naming the mechanism (wait on the background run thread captured from `_mcp_writes.spawn_context_daemon`, joined with a bound sized for a hang, not for slowness) and why it removes the host-load dependency.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: 'The test waits on the run's own completion signal or a state change, not a fixed 5-second wall clock'","ABSENCE: no section describes the mechanism (e.g. capturing the spawn_context_daemon thread and joining it with a bound) or why it removes the host-load dependency"],"finding":"The plan never names the chosen mechanism or gives a positive rationale for it. The first acceptance criterion leaves it open ('completion signal or a state change'), so the plan does not record why waiting on the run's own thread (or another completion signal) is the right fit instead of a state-poll loop with a larger budget.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1f834eefb01f6f52","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan body (no Approach/Rationale section); Acceptance Criteria line 1","norm_id":"n2fffb510c2abf1e6","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future implementer or reader satisfies the 'state change' branch with a poll loop that has a longer deadline, which keeps a wall-clock dependency and lets the flake come back under heavier load"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add: 'Approach: spy on rebar._mcp_writes.spawn_context_daemon to capture the run thread, join it with a generous bound that only catches a hung run (e.g. 120 s), assert it is no longer alive, then read the settled status. This ties the wait to the run actually finishing, so host load can slow it but cannot make it fail.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_